      "textEn": "34\nOf the one who is turned away from Krishna, by fate,\nOf the one who is afflicted by unrighteousness, of the sorrowful.\nFor the sake of grace, they walk, not the past,\nThe future, O Janardana. 3). Shabdartham\nJanasya- of a common person; Krishnat- from Lord Krishna; Vimukhasya- of one who turns away; Daivat- from the influence of Maya; Adharmaschalasya- of one engaged in unrighteousness; Su- always sorrowful; Dukhitasya- of one who is always sorrowful; Anugrahahya- for their benevolence; Karanaha; Iha- in this world; Charanti- wandering; Nunam- certainly; Bhutani- people; Bhavyan- extremely benevolent; Aatmanaha; Janardanasya- of Lord..\nOh Lord, great benevolent souls, from the side of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, wander on earth to show compassion to those fallen\nsouls who remain averse even to the mere thought of being subject to God. Meaning: To be obedient to God's will is the natural state of every being. But,\ndue to past misdeeds, the soul turns away from the thought of being subordinate to God and suffers all the sufferings of the material\nworld.\nNo one needs to do anything other than devotional service to Lord Krishna.\nNo one needs to do anything else. Therefore, any action other than divine love and devotion to God is supremely\nagainst one's will. All actions with desires, the experienceable vision, and the subordination to the Lord of Yoga—\nare contrary to the feeling of less or more, and the being who is engaged in such rebellious actions is often rejected by those\nrules of nature that are subject to the Lord. The great pure devotees of God\nare compassionate towards the fallen, therefore they keep wandering throughout the world with the aim of bringing souls back to the abode of God. Thus, to redeem such pure devotees of God, who are fallen souls, they go to them with the message of God. Therefore, a common person, who is affected by the external power of God,\nshould take advantage of their company. May that evil doer be destroyed.\nProtected by the Lord, the man. He who is situated in the heart, is full of devotion.\nKnowledge, the realization of the essence, is ancient. 4>."
