      "textEn": "36\nThey are deprived of direct cooperation from God. ©. When after many births, such non-dualists come to the realization\nthat God is worthy of worship and the devotee is different from God, only then can they take refuge in Lord Vasudeva.\nPure devotional practice begins from this point. By the Digambara Atwatvadi,\nthe method adopted to understand the ultimate truth is extremely difficult, whereas the method of devotion to understand the ultimate truth comes directly from God, because they are pleased with devotional service. As soon as Vidur arrived, he inquired from Maitreya on behalf of many newly initiated devotees about the path of devotional service,\nso that the Lord residing within the heart could be pleased.\nHaving performed actions, the incarnation is done.\nThat which is the self-energized divine power.\nAs it is created, this is without desire.\nHaving established the world's occupation. 500/-. Meaning of the word\n\nKaroti-- does; Karmani-- divine deeds; Krita- accepting; Avatarah-- incarnation; Yani- all these; Atma- Tanrah- independent;\nBhagavan-- God; Tri-adhishah-- lords of the three worlds; Yatha- as; Sasarj- created; Agre- first; Idam- this;\nThis vast world; Nirihah- though without desire; Sanstapya- by establishing; Vrittim- means of livelihood; Jagat- of the universe; Vidhatta- in the way he regulates. Oh, great sage, please tell us how the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is desireless in the three worlds,\nis the independent master and the controller of all powers, how he accepts incarnations, and\nhow he creates the vast universe, for the sake of which the regulating principle is fully\nsystematically arranged.\n\nMeaning: Lord Krishna is the first Lord, from whom, due to the cause of the universe, Vishnu, the one who resides in the womb, Vishnu, and\nVishnu in his Rudra form, the three terrible avatars of Vishnu expand. The entire physical creation is operated by three men in three stages, respectively, under the external power of God, and in this way,\nthe physical nature is controlled by them. To consider physical nature as independent is just like\ndiscovering milk in goat's udders. God is independent and desireless §. They do not create the physical world\nfor their own satisfaction, just as we create domestic\nwork for the fulfillment of our physical desires. In reality, the physical world is created for the enjoyment of the delusions of those bound beings"
