      "textEn": "37\nIt is done, those who have been against the divine service of God since time immemorial. But the physical\nuniverse is complete in itself. In the physical world, there is no lack of sustenance. Due to lack of knowledge,\nphysicalists are disturbed when there is a showy increase in the population on Earth. But whenever any creature comes to Earth, God immediately arranges for their livelihood.\nHe does. Other wombs, whose number is far greater than human society, are never worried about sustenance.\nThey are not. They are never seen dying of hunger. This is the only human society that is concerned about the food\nsituation, and to hide the administrative disorder, this argument is given\nthat the population is increasing at an excessive rate. If there is any lack in the world, then it is the lack of divine consciousness.\nOtherwise, by the grace of God, there is no lack of anything.\nAs again, this is invested.\nIn the cave, he retires.\nThe lord of Yogeshwara, one, this-\nTANTS, often as it is. 6>. Meaning of the word\nYatha--as; Punah--again; Swayam--in oneself; Khe-in the form of sky; Idam--this; Nivat-in entering;\nShote- one who sleeps; Guhayam- within the universe; Sah-he (God); Nivrutt- without effort; Vritti- means of livelihood;\nYoga- master of all yogic powers; Adhishwarah- master of all things; Ekah- unique; Etat- this;\nAnupravishta- one who enters later; Bahad- in countless ways; Yatha- in the manner; Aasit- exists..\nThey spread in the form of the sky, lie down in their own heart, and keeping the entire creation in that sky, they expand themselves in many beings, which appear in the form of different species. They do not have to make any effort for their livelihood because they are the master of all compound powers\nand the owner of every object.\nThus, they are different from living beings. Meaning: Questions regarding creation, sustenance, and destruction, which are mentioned in many parts of the Shrimad Bhagavat,\nare related to various kalpas (aeons); therefore, when questions are asked by various inquisitive people, their descriptions have been in different\nforms by various authorities. There is no disagreement regarding the principles of creation and the control of God over them, but due to being in different eras, there remains some difference in their subtleties.\nThere remains some difference. The immense sky is the physical body of God, which is called the immense form"
