      "textEn": "38\nAnd all material creations are situated in the sky, that is, in the heart of God. Therefore, from the sky\nto the gross sight, which is the first physical expression, every object up to the earth is called Brahma. All knowledge is nothing but Brahman, God, and they are one. The living being is supreme power,\nwhile the non-living is powerless, and from the combination of these two powers, this physical world is manifested,\nwhich is situated in the heart of God. Those who are endowed with wisdom, the twice-born,\nFor the protection of the world, they are the incarnations of actions.\nEven if the mind is not satisfied, listen to these verses.\nThey are the nectar of the stories of Sushruta and Mareecha. 7/. Meaning of the word\n\nPlaying with play; Vidhatte- creates; Dwija- born as a twice-born; Gau- cow; Suranam- of the gods; Ksayam- for welfare; Karmani- divine actions; Avatar- incarnation; Bhedaih- separately; Manah- mind; Na- never; Tupyati- is satisfied; Api- despite; Shrunvatam- constantly listening; Nah- ours; Su- auspicious, auspicious; Maulih- of God\nCharacteristic; Amritani-- immortal \\.\n\nYou, twice-born, for the welfare of cows and gods, also describe the auspicious\ncharacteristics of various incarnations of God. Although we constantly hear about their divine activities,\nour minds are never completely satisfied. Meaning: God appears in this universe in various incarnations, such as Matsya, Kurma, Varaha, and Narasimha.\nIn these forms, he manifests and performs various divine tasks for the welfare of Brahmins, cows, and gods.\nGod directly cares for Brahmins, meaning civilized men. A civilized person is one,\nwho has taken birth twice. The living being is born in this world from the union of male and female. Man\nis born from the union of parents, but the second birth of a civilized man occurs through the contact of a guru,\nwho becomes the real father.\nParents who provide the physical body are only for one birth.\nParents are, 